    "The NgramRL system enhances reinforcement learning (RL) post-training by using a rollout-aware n-gram caching mechanism.",
    "This approach addresses the high computational costs associated with rollout generation during RL post-training.",
    "NgramRL is particularly relevant in the context of Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO).",
    "NgramRL maintains a per-prompt n-gram cache built from prior rollouts of the same prompt.",
    "The n-gram cache allows the system to propose draft continuations based on previously generated outputs.",
    "NgramRL leverages the temporal locality of prompts.",
    "Across consecutive epochs, prior rollouts can cover 48-96% of later rollouts, indicating significant redundancy.",
    "NgramRL exploits this redundancy to improve efficiency.",
    "During each training step, NgramRL proposes draft tokens from the n-gram cache.",
    "These draft tokens are verified by the policy in a single forward pass.",
    "The draft-and-verify mechanism ensures alignment with the evolving policy.",
    "The cache is populated with the policy's own outputs to prevent staleness.",
    "NgramRL operates without adding persistent GPU memory.",
    "It does not require auxiliary model training.",
    "The cache resides in host memory and is queried on the CPU.",
    "CPU querying overlaps with GPU computation, minimizing additional GPU time for drafting.",
    "NgramRL incorporates an adaptive fan-out prefetcher that speculatively prepares drafts for likely verification outcomes.",
    "The prefetching mechanism keeps the cache off the critical path of decoding.",
    "This allows for faster processing and reduces overall rollout time.",
    "NgramRL commits 3.60-7.77 tokens per target-model forward.",
    "This is up to 1.99 times more than traditional SuffixDecoding methods.",
    "It is 7.0 times more than prompt-lookup decoding.",
    "The prefetcher can deliver up to 1.38 times the measured rollout speedup compared to synchronous execution.",
    "NgramRL reduces computational costs in RL post-training.",
    "It improves efficiency and maintains alignment with the evolving policy.",
    "The draft-and-verify mechanism combined with adaptive prefetching accelerates rollout generation.",
    "NgramRL preserves the accuracy and convergence of the training process.",
    "NgramRL is a valuable optimization in RL-style setups where prompts recur."
] 

