    "The key components of ExpertFlow that contribute to this reduction are the Routing Path Predictor (RPP), Token Scheduler, and Predictive Expert Cache.",
    "The Routing Path Predictor (RPP) is a transformer-based component that estimates expert usage across all MoE layers in a single forward pass.",
    "The RPP accurately predicts which experts will be needed for a given input.",
    "Accurate prediction by the RPP enables more efficient expert loading and execution, minimizing unnecessary memory usage.",
    "The Token Scheduler groups tokens with similar predicted routes to improve expert utilization.",
    "Scheduling tokens based on their predicted expert requirements reduces the number of experts activated simultaneously.",
    "Reducing the number of simultaneously activated experts leads to lower memory consumption.",
    "The Predictive Expert Cache loads only the required experts while correcting any mispredictions at runtime.",
    "The dynamic caching mechanism of the Predictive Expert Cache ensures only necessary experts are kept in GPU memory.",
    "Keeping only necessary experts in GPU memory reduces the overall memory footprint.",
    "Together, these components enable ExpertFlow to achieve up to 93.72% peak memory reduction compared to existing offloading baselines on a single GPU.",
    "ExpertFlow improves inference throughput by up to 10 times compared to existing offloading baselines on a single GPU.",
    "These innovations address challenges of low expert utilization, inefficient expert prediction, and ineffective expert caching common in traditional MoE implementations.",
    "ExpertFlow integrates these methods to provide a unified system that enhances memory efficiency and performance in MoE architectures.",
    "The improvements and results are detailed in the paper titled "ExpertFlow: Efficient Mixture-of-Experts Inference via Predictive Expert Caching and Token Scheduling," arXiv:2410.17954v2."
] 

