Statements:
[
    "ExpertFlow introduces three synergistic components that enhance the efficiency of Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) inference while addressing memory constraints.",
    "The first component is the Routing Path Predictor (RPP), which is transformer-based and estimates expert usage across all MoE layers in a single forward pass.",
    "The RPP accurately predicts which experts will be activated for given tokens.",
    "The RPP facilitates better scheduling and prefetching of experts, improving overall efficiency and reducing memory usage.",
    "The second component is the Token Scheduler, which groups tokens with similar predicted routes to enhance expert utilization.",
    "The Token Scheduler optimizes token processing based on routing patterns.",
    "The Token Scheduler minimizes the number of experts that need to be activated simultaneously, alleviating memory pressure.",
    "The third component is the Predictive Expert Cache, which dynamically loads only the required experts and corrects mispredictions at runtime.",
    "The Predictive Expert Cache ensures only necessary experts are kept in memory, reducing GPU memory usage.",
    "The Predictive Expert Cache improves the efficiency of expert loading and execution.",
    "Together, these components enable ExpertFlow to reduce GPU memory usage by up to 93.72%.",
    "ExpertFlow improves inference throughput by up to 10 times compared to existing offloading methods (arXiv:2410.17954v2).",
    "This coordinated approach addresses challenges of low expert utilization, inefficient expert prediction, and ineffective expert caching in traditional MoE models."
] 

