Statements:
[
    "PAC-MAN integrates safety and perception constraints for effective humanoid dodgeball evasion through a combination of control barrier functions (CBFs) and a perception-aware reinforcement learning (RL) framework.",
    "The central challenge addressed by PAC-MAN is the need for a humanoid robot to avoid contact with an incoming ball while maintaining balance, using only limited onboard sensing capabilities.",
    "The PAC-MAN framework utilizes a head-mounted depth camera to perceive the incoming ball.",
    "The robot's policy operates under the constraint that it cannot access the ball's state directly; instead, it must infer information about the ball from depth observations.",
    "This setup models the task as a partially observed Markov decision process, where the robot must react quickly to avoid being struck.",
    "CBFs are employed to encode safety constraints by defining collision-free sets and correcting unsafe commands.",
    "The framework distinguishes between two levels of barrier guidance: Link-CBF and Joint-CBF.",
    "Link-CBF provides lightweight per-link rewards during training.",
    "Joint-CBF offers a stronger whole-body joint-space projection that can guide training or be used as a runtime filter.",
    "The effectiveness of these CBFs is contingent on the quality of the perceptual input.",
    "Stronger barrier structures require more informative observations.",
    "PAC-MAN incorporates an adversarial motion prior (AMP) to regularize the humanoid's evasive movements.",
    "The AMP encourages the robot to adopt reflex-like evasive actions such as crouching, leaning, and sidestepping.",
    "The AMP is trained using a discriminator that distinguishes between policy-generated transitions and human-derived motion clips.",
    "The training process employs Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) across multiple parallel environments.",
    "The robot learns effective evasive strategies in a simulated setting before deployment on a physical robot.",
    "The PAC-MAN framework achieves high success rates in evading throws, even under conditions of imperfect perception.",
    "The Link-CBF policy achieves a 95% success rate in real-world tests.",
    "The usability of barrier structures is heavily influenced by perceptual observability.",
    "The Joint-CBF performs best with accurate ball state information.",
    "The Link-CBF is more suitable for deployment under limited perception conditions.",
    "Integrating perception capabilities with safety mechanisms enhances the robot's evasive performance.",
    "PAC-MAN leverages CBFs to ensure collision avoidance.",
    "PAC-MAN employs an AMP to guide motion.",
    "PAC-MAN adapts its strategies based on the quality of perceptual input.",
    "This holistic approach enables the humanoid robot to perform evasive maneuvers in a dynamic environment.",
    "PAC-MAN demonstrates the potential for safe and responsive robotic interactions with moving objects."
] 

